# Lint policy for tests/: the root .clang-tidy, with two differences.
#
# HeaderFilterRegex adds the shared support headers to the root's lib/cli/ext.
# A suite reaches them through its parent directory, so clang-tidy sees
# tests/unit/../support/<name>.hpp rather than tests/support/<name>.hpp, and
# the pattern matches on the directory name. The tools/analysis headers two
# tests include the same way (tests/unit/../../tools/analysis/...) stay out,
# as they are for the analysis tools' own sources under the root pattern.
#
# bugprone-unchecked-optional-access is off, because Catch2's REQUIRE is
# invisible to it. The check is a flow analysis: it accepts `if (!x) return;`
# before `*x`, and `if (!x) { FAIL(...); }` (FAIL ends in
# Catch::Detail::Unreachable()), but REQUIRE stops a case only when it fails,
# by throwing from inside Catch2's AssertionHandler, which the analysis cannot
# see, so it follows the failing branch on into the access. `.value()` does
# not help; the check counts it as an access too. Measured with clang-tidy 18
# over every tests/ source, it reported 67 accesses, 62 of them correct:
#   48  `REQUIRE(x.has_value())` (or `REQUIRE(x)`), then `*x`;
#   10  guarded by an `if` or `continue` the analysis lost: 2 because the
#       optional is reached through a call (`points[k].value`), 8 on a local
#       inside loops (both shapes reproduce in a dozen-line function);
#    4  guarded by an invariant another class enforces (the legacy surface
#       Decoder throws on a noise_threshold without a noise, so
#       `noiseOf(i) >= 0` implies the noise is there);
#    5  real, and fixed in the commit that wrote this: four `cells()->`
#       read the very lattice their case is checking, now `.value()`, so an
#       empty one fails the CHECK instead of being undefined behaviour; one
#       `*b` was guarded by a CHECK that carries on when it fails, now a
#       REQUIRE, as vanilla_freeze_test.cpp already has it.
# Keeping it on would mean rewriting the 48 REQUIREs as if/FAIL, which moves
# every such case's assertion count (a REQUIRE that holds is an assertion; an
# `if` that does not fire is none), and a NOLINT on each of the other 14.
# ext/tests sit under the root config, where the check stays on (they trip
# it nowhere).
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: '-bugprone-unchecked-optional-access'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/((lib|cli|ext)/.*|support/[^/]*)\.(hpp|h)$'
